sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2019-boundary-20> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Cognitive light cones grow or shrink as an agent's organization changes, and the key is a balance of selective information sharing through \"synapses\" (any structures that gate signals based on the state of others): too little sharing fails to bind subunits into a new Self, and too much yields an undifferentiated soup without modules or layered abstraction.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Selves form only at intermediate levels of information sharing between subunits";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “The Computational Boundary of a \"Self\": Developmental Bioelectricity Drives Multicellularity and Scale-Free Cognition”, Frontiers in psychology (2019), doi:10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688; section “Conclusion and Future Outlook”. Scope: Multicellular and multi-agent biological systems"
}
